@startuml clock_mapping
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
title Which clock setting labels the measurement end, and when is it frozen? (not to scale)
concise "Measurement\n(kernel monotonic time)" as Measurement
concise "Case 1: anchor before the end\nqualifies at admission" as Before
concise "Case 2: no qualifying anchor\nat admission" as After
concise "Case 3: no qualifying anchor\nby the deadline" as None
concise "Device real-time clock\n(UTC, set by SNTP)" as Clock
hide time-axis
scale 1 as 16 pixels
@0
Measurement is Idle
Before is "Idle setup applies anchor A"
After is "anchor A older than 12.5 h before the end"
None is "no anchor, or every anchor too far"
Clock is "set by anchor A"
@12
Before is "A within 12.5 h of the end"
@20
Measurement is "acquisition start ... end"
@40
Measurement is Finalizing
@48
Measurement is "job admitted"
Before is "freeze at admission"
After is "delivery SNTP: anchor B"
None is "delivery setup fails or anchor not usable"
@60
Measurement is "delivery attempts"
Before is "frozen: same UTC end, Device id, bytes"
@64
After is "freeze before first request"
@76
After is "frozen: same UTC end, Device id, bytes"
@80
Clock is "later SNTP exchange steps the clock"
@82
Measurement is {-}
None is "deadline: SERVER_CONNECTION_FAILURE"
@100
Measurement@20 <-> @40 : listening: monotonic duration, never relabelled
note bottom of Before
 UTC end = anchor UTC + (measurement end - anchor monotonic time).
 An anchor qualifies only if |measurement end - anchor| <= 12.5 h,
 that is (1 s - 100 ms) / 20 ppm; it may lie before or after the end.
 Case 3 sends nothing.
end note
note bottom of Clock
 Frozen exactly once: later exchanges, retries and backward or forward
 clock steps never change the frozen UTC end, identifier or body bytes.
end note
@enduml
